## Golden rules
1. The LLM acts only through tools. It never writes state directly.
2. Every draft field records `source` (user | derived | verified | default) and `confirmed`. Derived and verified values must be confirmed by the user before submit.
3. Submit rules are enforced in code (`can_submit`, the guard node and the `submit_inquiry` tool), never trusted to the LLM.
4. Consent (`terms_accepted`) can only be set by a UI action from the review card, never by the LLM.
5. Documents: only check presence, extension and size (5 MB). Never read or analyse file content.
6. All external systems (CR verify, email link, OTP, storage, submit, status) are mocks behind interfaces in `backend/app/services/`.
7. Mall, unit-type and FAQ answers come only from seeded data in `backend/app/data/`. Never invent facts.
8. Never log OTP codes, uploaded file contents or full contact details at INFO level.

## Conventions
- Small, focused modules; type everything (TypeScript strict, Python type hints + mypy-friendly).
- Tests alongside each step; keep them green before moving on.
- No new dependencies beyond the stack above without stating why.
- Commands: `make dev`, `make test`, `make lint` (root Makefile).
